## 6. User Journeys and Use Cases

### 6.1 The Golden Path (Primary Journey)

This is the rehearsed demo scenario. It must work every time.

| Step | What happens | What the audience sees |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | The scripted attack sequence replays up to the point where "Node A" is confirmed compromised | Detection fires; the attack-path graph draws itself live on the 3D console |
| 2 | The system produces a forecast | "Precog predicts Server B is the next target — 74% confidence" as a glowing forecast cone on the 3D graph, and pushed to the phone |
| 3 | The analyst taps **Contain** on the phone | A confirmation is shown, then accepted |
| 4 | The replay resumes | The scripted next event (a move toward Server B) is shown as blocked; the attack chain is shown ending early |
| 5 | The accuracy counter updates | "Precog accuracy this session" ticks up |

(The 74% figure is illustrative.)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant R as Replay feed
    participant P as Pipeline
    participant B as Backend
    participant C as 3D Console
    participant M as Phone App
    participant A as Analyst
    R->>P: Attack events
    P->>B: Node A confirmed compromised
    B->>C: Graph update
    B->>M: Alert + graph summary
    P->>B: Forecast (Top-3, confidence)
    B->>C: Forecast cones
    B->>M: Forecast + Contain button
    A->>M: Tap Contain
    M->>B: Contain request (confirmed)
    B->>P: Simulated containment
    R->>P: Next scripted event (toward Server B)
    P->>B: Event blocked
    B->>C: Attack chain ended early
    B->>M: Accuracy counter updated
```

