## 9. Data Requirements

### 9.1 Data Sources

| Source | Use | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| CICIDS2017 | Training, testing and replay events | Public research dataset |
| Scripted attack logs | Golden path and Precog training sequences | Internally generated; formatted to resemble Caldera and Atomic Red Team output |
| MITRE ATT&CK data (`mitre-attack/attack-stix-data`) | Technique names and tactics for the techniques the project uses | Public framework data, used under MITRE's ATT&CK Terms of Use (copyright notice kept with the data) |

### 9.2 Data Entities (Product Level)

| Entity | Purpose | Key fields (product level) |
|---|---|---|
| **Packet record** | One replayed network packet stored by NIDS | Source host (IP address), destination host (IP address), timestamp, protocol, ports, size, flags |
| **Feature vector (offline)** | Input to the offline CICIDS2017 model | Features taken from CICIDS2017 |
| **Detection** | Result of NIDS's detector | Packet reference, anomaly flag, risk score (0 to 100), severity (HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW or NORMAL) |
| **Security event** | Normalized detection | Identity, timestamp, severity, explanation, ATT&CK technique if matched |
| **Host (node)** | One machine on the graph | Identifier, name, state (normal, compromised, contained) |
| **Connection (edge)** | Observed link between hosts | Source host, destination host, time observed |
| **Attack graph snapshot** | Current graph state | Hosts, connections, states |
| **Forecast** | Precog output | Current compromised node, Top-3 targets, confidence per target, source of the forecast, timestamp, outcome (pending, hit, miss) |
| **Containment action** | Simulated response | Target node, requesting client, confirmation, timestamp, result |
| **Audit log entry** | Record of what happened | Timestamp, type (detection, forecast, containment), reference |
| **Session record** | Per-session summary | Forecasts and outcomes, hit-rate, containment results |
| **Demo user** | Mocked login | Demo account only |

The exact field names and types are fixed in the TRD and in the schemas in `contracts/`.

### 9.3 Data Quality and Governance

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| **DR-1** | Training and replay data shall be traceable to CICIDS2017 or to the scripted logs |
| **DR-2** | Feature extraction shall be identical for training and replay |
| **DR-3** | Class imbalance shall be handled and documented |
| **DR-4** | No real personal data shall appear in any dataset, log or screen |
| **DR-5** | Session and audit data are held for the demo only; no long-term retention is required |

### 9.4 Data Contracts Between Roles

| ID | Requirement |
|---|---|
| **DC-1** | Every data format passed between roles shall have a formal JSON Schema and sample JSON in `contracts/` |
| **DC-2** | Each role shall build and test against the sample JSON first, then swap in real data without changing its own code |
| **DC-3** | A change to a contract shall be made only through LEAD-CORE, and all roles shall be told |

Contracts needed, at minimum: packet record, detection, security event, attack graph snapshot, forecast, containment action, replay status, and session record.

