## 15. Acceptance Criteria and Definition of Done

### 15.1 Product-Level Acceptance

The product is accepted when all of the following are true:

| # | Criterion |
|---|---|
| **AC-1** | The golden path runs from start to finish on localhost: replayed event, detection, attack graph, ATT&CK context, Precog forecast, 3D visualization, mobile alert, analyst containment, re-evaluation |
| **AC-2** | Detection performance is measured on a held-out portion of CICIDS2017 and reported with precision, recall, F1 and false-positive rate |
| **AC-3** | The Precog Engine produces Top-3 forecasts with confidence, and reports precision@k, a calibration curve and containment success rate |
| **AC-4** | The live accuracy counter is visible and updates correctly |
| **AC-5** | The mobile web app installs on a phone and shows live alerts and executes a containment action |
| **AC-6** | No containment executes without human confirmation |
| **AC-7** | No live attack or real enforcement was ever run |
| **AC-8** | The golden path ran without failure in 5 consecutive rehearsals (Proposed, see SM-5) |
| **AC-9** | A recorded backup video of a perfect run exists |
| **AC-10** | The IEEE paper is scoped to the Precog contribution, with a literature-search-backed novelty claim |
| **AC-11** | Every Must requirement in Section 7 passes its acceptance criterion |

### 15.2 Definition of Done (Per Requirement)

A requirement is done only when:

1. The code or file exists in the owner's folder and runs without errors.
2. It has been tested against its acceptance criterion, with the result noted.
3. It was committed to the owner's branch and LEAD-CORE was asked to merge.
4. LEAD-CORE merged it and confirmed that `main` still runs.
5. Any contract it uses matches the files in `contracts/`.

### 15.3 Test Approach

| Level | What is tested | By whom |
|---|---|---|
| Unit | Each module alone against sample data | Each role owner |
| Component | Model quality (detection and Precog) with the evaluation in Section 10 | DETECT, LEAD-CORE |
| Integration | Modules connected through the backend | LEAD-CORE |
| End-to-end | The full golden path | LEAD-CORE, with all roles |
| Device | The installed app on real phones | GRAPH, with LEAD-CORE |
| Rehearsal | Repeated full demo runs | All |

